# 27. WEEK 26
# Grammar, Usage & Punctuation

## Core Objectives

Students will:

- maintain subject-verb agreement;
- maintain consistent verb tense;
- use clear pronoun references;
- recognize sentence boundaries;
- use commas;
- use apostrophes;
- select appropriate punctuation.

## Instructional Principle

Rules should be explained before memory shortcuts are introduced.

Students should understand what punctuation communicates or separates.

## Subject-Verb Agreement

The subject and verb must agree in number.

Example:

The student **writes**.

The students **write**.

## Verb Tense

Verb tense should accurately communicate time and remain consistent unless the time changes.

## Pronoun Clarity

A pronoun should clearly refer to a specific noun.

Students should avoid references where the reader cannot determine who or what the pronoun represents.

## ACT Alignment

- Conventions of Standard English

