## Data Interpretation Process

1. Read the title.
2. Identify variables.
3. Identify units.
4. Determine what information changes.
5. Locate the requested values.
6. Compare values if needed.
7. Draw only conclusions supported by the data.

## Common Error

Students may interpret what they expect a graph to show instead of what it actually shows.

Instruction should repeatedly return students to the displayed data.

