# 48. GUIDED NOTES DESIGN

Guided notes should reduce unnecessary copying while still requiring students to process information.

Notes may include:

- partially completed definitions;
- labeled examples;
- worked examples;
- places to complete calculations;
- short written explanations;
- check-your-understanding questions;
- retrieval questions.

Students should not spend most of the instructional period copying slides word-for-word.

